xnu 0174: boot bisection marks and the log before vfs_mountroot

Two things cost a whole afternoon on 2026-10-28: the boot stopped before
the UFS probe left anything on disk, and the only clue was a screen with
the last early mark. Keep a mondrianstop=N boot argument that halts at
early stage N with IRQs masked, extend the early marks through bsd_init
and vfs_mountroot, and let marks above 20 draw after the console has been
switched off. Arm the persistent console ring as soon as the UFS probe
knows the partition, not after the root mount: a failed mount then leaves
the mount error in the ring instead of in RAM. The mark blocks are clamped
to the framebuffer width so a stage past 25 cannot write outside it.

